※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4934 LANG_TABLE_HANDED_TO_A_FILLER

※ A parameter whose type is a writable table is one the function may fill, and
※ filling it is no effect of the function's: its signature says so, and what it
※ changes is what it was handed.  Whether that is an effect is the caller's
※ question.  A table is a handle, so the one at the top level handed over here
※ is the one every other function reads, and a pure function does not hand it
※ to be filled -- where one it made itself it may.

let std := ⎕import("std")

let kept: mut ⸨str: u8⸩ = ⸨⸩

fn filled(d: mut ⸨str: u8⸩) → u8:
    d⸨"a"⸩ ← 1u8
    1u8

fn spread() → u8:
    filled(kept)

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if spread() = 1u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
